  "worked_solution": "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(x)={f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(-3)={f}^{\u2032}(-3)\\cdot g(-3)+f(-3)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-3).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-3)=-2$ and $g(-3)=0.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,2)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(-3)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,-2)$ equals $3.$ So, ${g}^{\u2032}(-3)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(-3) & ={f}^{\u2032}(-3)\\cdot g(-3)+f(-3)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
